          "tool_output": "Q3 REVIEW MEETING \u2014 MEETING NOTES\n==================================\nDate:      Monday, September 8, 2026\nTime:      10:00 \u2013 11:30 am PT (Zoom)\nFacilitator: Rachel Kim\n\nATTENDEES\n---------\nRachel Kim        (VP of Sales)\nClaire Fontaine   (CFO)\nPriya Nair        (CTO)\nHannah Park       (Head of Product)\nKenji Obi         (HR Manager)\nJames Okafor      (Account Executive)\nSofia Delgado     (Account Executive)\nDaniel Torres     (Product Manager)\nOscar Mensah      (Finance Analyst)\n\nAGENDA\n------\n1. Q3 Sales Review\n2. Engineering & Product Update\n3. Finance Snapshot\n4. HR Update\n5. Action Items / Q4 Planning\n\n---\n\n1. Q3 SALES REVIEW\n-------------------\nRachel Kim opened with a summary of Q3 performance.\n\n- Total revenue closed (won deals): $1,040,000 across 14 closed-won deals.\n- 22 total deals worked in the quarter; win rate 63.6%.\n- South region led all territories at $468,000 in closed revenue.\n- Largest single deal: D019 \u2014 Sofia Delgado \u2014 $198,000 \u2014 Meridian Insights Pro\n  (signed September 5, Southern enterprise account).\n- Pipeline carry-over into Q4: D007 ($7,800), D013 ($105,000), D020 ($115,000),\n  D022 ($11,000) \u2014 total pending ~$239,300.\n\nJames Okafor noted that the North region pipeline is especially strong heading into Q4,\nwith two new prospects from the BostonTech conference (see EX001 travel expense).\n\nAction: Rachel to circulate updated forecast by EOD September 9.\n\n2. ENGINEERING & PRODUCT UPDATE\n---------------------------------\nPriya Nair reported that the DataBridge connector reached 28/30 license utilisation\n(SKU-003) and a capacity upgrade is under evaluation for Q4.\n\nHannah Park flagged that Custom Dashboard Builder (SKU-009) is at 22/25 seats; renewal\nin February 2027 should include a seat expansion.\n\nDaniel Torres confirmed the new Meridian Connector - REST (SKU-005) rollout is complete.\nEleven of twenty available licenses are now provi